T18:19:41Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T19:49:50Z","closed_at":"2026-08-26T19:39:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117938","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117938","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117938.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117938.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-26T19:39:27Z"},"body":"- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5453\r\n\r\nWhat Feral GameMode does is pretty much explained in the proposal above.\r\n\r\nWhether GameMode is used or not is determined by a new \"Use Game Mode\" project setting.\r\n\r\nThe current implementation waits for main loop initialization (so it can determine if it's running from the editor and get the project setting), then it requests the GameMode daemon to activate using its process ID right after the main loop is initialized. A verbose warning is emitted if GameMode fails to start (possibly due to not being available).\r\n\r\nAfter the main loop is finalized, it requests the daemon to end if starting was successful.\r\n\r\nGameMode will not be activated in the following cases:\r\n- Inside the editor (a project running inside still works).\r\n- At the project manager (has to be checked since the setting is treated as enabled).\r\n\r\nA namespace for `gamemode_client.h` has to be used since including it directly causes conflicts with zlib.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users